hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5827","narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) did not seek omens from anything. However, it was his practice that when he would come to a place, he would inquire about the name of that place. If its name was good, its effect would be visible on his face, and if its name was bad, that effect would also be visible on his face."
"5828","narrates: My father's name was Aziz, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) changed his name to Abdur Rahman."
"5829","The name of Sayyidah Juwayriyyah bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) was previously Barrah, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) named her Juwayriyyah."
"5830","""Zainab used to be called ""Barrah"" (good), and it was said that she was praising herself. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed her name to Zainab."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3732)"
"5831","Do not say al-karm (for the word vine) but say al-habala (that is grape). (Using translation from Muslim 2248a)"
"5832","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Do not call grapes 'karm' because 'karm' is a Muslim person."
"5833","Do not use the word karm (for wine) for worthy of respect is the heart of a believer. (Using translation from Muslim 2247b)"
"5834","None of you should use the word al-harin (for grape) for the heart of a believer is karm (worthy of respect). (Using translation from Muslim 2247d)"
"5835","The worst name in the sight of Allah Almighty is that a person is called 'King of Kings'."" (The narrator says:) That is, he is called 'Shahanshah' (Emperor)."
"5836","Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to give names to our servants as these four names: Aflah (Successful), Rabdh (Profit), Yasar (Wealth), and Nafi' (Beneficial). (Using translation from Muslim 2136a)"
"5837","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not name your slave Aflah, Najeeh, Rabah, or Yasar. You should consider that you do not add anything to it."
"5838","Do not call your servant Yasar (wealth), Rabah (profit), Nijih(prosperous) and Aflah (successful), for you may ask; Is he there? And someone says: No. Samurah said: These are four (names), so do not attribute more to me. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4958)"
"5839","The narrator says) I do not know whether the word Aflah is in the narration or not. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, but he had not prohibited this. After that, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to prohibit it, but then he also left it."
"5840","Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided to forbid (his followers) to name persons as Ya'la (Elevated), Baraka (Blessing), Aflah (Successful), Yasar and Nafi', but I saw that he kept silent after that and he did not say anything until Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. And he did not forbid (his followers to do this), then 'Umar decided to prohibit (people) from giving these names, but later on gave up the idea. (Using translation from Muslim 2138)"
"5841","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If I remain alive, I will prohibit people from naming their children Rabah, Najeeh, Aflah, and Yasar."
"5842","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to prohibit naming with Maymun, Barakah, Aflah, or any other similar name, but then he (peace be upon him) abandoned this intention."
"5843","I had a curtain on which there was a picture; I had hung it over a niche. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took hold of it and pulled it down and said, ""Are you putting up a curtain on the wall?"" I made two cushions out of that cloth. Then I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) reclining on them (that is, he did not forbid its use in this way)."
"5844","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade placing pictures in houses."
"5845","Messenger of Allah, I offer repentance to Allah and His Messenger. (but tell me) what is the sin that I have committed. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What is this carpet? She said: I bought it for you so that you might sit on it and take rest. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The owners of these pictures would be tormented and they would be asked to bring to life what they tried to create. He then said: Angels do not enter the house in which there is a picture. (Using translation from Muslim 2107n)"
"5846","The narrator states: That person went away; he had mentioned that he had children (for whom he earned a livelihood in this way), so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Do not make any picture that is of a living thing."
"5847","The face of the Prophet (peace be upon him) changed color, and he moved towards the curtain and removed it with his blessed hand. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, those who make pictures of Allah’s creation will face severe punishment."
"5848","I was sitting with Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) when a man came to him and said: I am a person whose livelihood depends on making pictures. Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: I heard Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""Whoever makes a picture, Allah will punish him by commanding him to put a soul into it, and he will not be able to put a soul into it."" Upon hearing this, the man's face turned pale, so Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: If you must make pictures, then make pictures of trees or anything that does not have a soul."
"5849","that Rafi' bin Ishaq informed him, saying: ""I and 'Abdullah bin Abi Talhah entered upon Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri to visit him. So Abu Sa'eed said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us: ""The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image or a picture."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2805)"
"5850","I said to Ubaidullah Khawlani: Did he not narrate to us the hadith (about the picture), and yet he has put up this cloth? So Ubaidullah said: Did you not hear him say that the ruling regarding designs on cloth is different (i.e., it is permitted)?"
"5851","From 'Ubaidullah bin 'Abdullah bin 'Utbah, that he entered upon Abu Talhah Al-Ansari to pay him a visit (while he was ill), and he found Sahl bin Hunaif with him. He said: ""Abu Talhah called for someone to remove a sheet that was under him. Sahl said to him: 'Why did you remove it?' He replied: 'Because it contains images on it, and the Prophet ﷺ said about them what you know.' Sahl said: 'Do he not say: Except for markings on a garment?' He said: 'Yes, but this is better to me.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1750)"
"5852","I saw my father, he bought a slave who performed cupping. He brought his cupping instruments, so they were broken. I asked him about this, and he told me: Indeed, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade the price of blood (i.e., the earnings from cupping), the price of a dog, and the income of a prostitute (from being used). And the Prophet (peace be upon him) cursed the woman who tattoos and the woman who gets tattooed, the one who consumes usury and the one who gives it, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) cursed the image-maker."
"5853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Come inside. He replied: We do not enter a house in which there are pictures. If you (peace and blessings be upon him) must use them in your house, then cut off their heads, or cut them and make cushions or mats out of them."
"5854","The narrator says:) There was a curtain in the house on which a picture was made, and there was also a dog in the house. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that the head of the picture be cut off, and regarding the curtain with pictures, he (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that the heads in the pictures be cut off, and that cushions be made from that cloth. According to his (peace and blessings be upon him) order, the dog was taken out; it was a puppy with which Sayyiduna Imam Hasan and Sayyiduna Imam Husain (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to play, and it was under their bed. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then Jibreel came to me, and after that he continuously advised me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"5855","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Angels do not enter the house in which there is a dog or a statue. (Using translation from Muslim 2106b)"
"5856","Messenger of Allah, I find a change in your mood today. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Gabriel had promised me that he would meet me tonight, but he did not meet me. By Allah, he never broke his promises, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the day in this sad (mood). Then it occurred to him that there had been a puppy under their cot. He commanded and it was turned out. He then took some water in his hand and sprinkled it at that place. When it was evening Gabriel met him and he said to him: you promised me that you would meet me the previous night. He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture. Then on that very morning he commanded the killing of the dogs until he announced that the dog kept for the orchards should also be killed, but he spared the dog meant for the protection of extensive fields (or big gardens). (Using translation from Muslim 2105)"
"5857","The Prophet ﷺ ordered Umar ibn al-Khattab who was in al-Batha' at the time of the conquest (of Makkah) to visit the Ka'bah and obliterate all images in it. The Prophet ﷺ did not enter it until all the images were obliterated. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4156)"
"5858","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: As for these people, they know this matter, that angels do not enter a house in which there is a picture. Here is the picture of Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him); when did he ever play dice?"
"5859","The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): They should try to create a grain, or produce a particle—here the words are in the imperative form, but what is meant by this is to render the opponent helpless."
"5860","I then tore it and prepared two cushions out of that. A person who was then in that company and whose name was Rabi'a b. 'Ata, the freed slave of Banu Zuhra, asked: Did you hear Abu Mabammad making a mention of A'isha having stated that Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recline upon them? lbn al-Qasim said: No, but I heard Qasim b. Muhammad saying so. (Using translation from Muslim 2107m)"
"5861","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw pictures inside the house (i.e., inside the Ka'bah), he did not enter it. Upon his command, they were erased. He saw in it a picture in which Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and Sayyiduna Ismail (peace be upon him) had arrows for divination in their hands. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: May Allah destroy these people! By Allah, these two noble ones never played with divining arrows."
"5862","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque, and at that time there were three hundred and sixty idols around it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began striking them with the stick he had in his hand, and he kept reciting: ""Truth has come and falsehood has vanished; indeed, falsehood is bound to vanish."
"5863","'A'isha reported that she used to play with dolls in the presence of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and when her playmates came to her they left (the house) because they felt shy of Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whereas Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them to her. (Using translation from Muslim 2440a)"
"5864","I was playing with a doll. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted the curtain and asked: O Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)! What is this? I replied: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! This is a doll. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: What is this thing between them? I replied: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! This is a horse. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Do cloth horses have wings? Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: Did not the horse of our master Sulaiman (peace be upon him) have wings? So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled."
"5865","I was playing with dolls."
"5866","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would send them back to me, so they would play with me."
"5867","narrates: Once some Abyssinians were displaying their war weapons with skill. During this, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived and threw pebbles at them. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umar, let them do it."
"5868","Abu Bakr, leave them alone for these are the days of 'Id. And 'A'isha said: I recapitulate to my mind the fact that once the Messenger of Allah ﷺ screened me with his mantle and I saw the sports of the Abyssinians, and I was only a girl, and so you can well imagine how a girl of tender age is fond of watching the sport. (Using translation from Muslim 892c)"
"5869","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to her during the days of Tashreeq. Two girls were sitting with her, singing and playing the daff. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) scolded them and tore their daff. Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Let them do it, for these are the days of Eid."
"5870","The Abyssinians used to perform acrobatics in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they would say things that were not understood. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""What are they saying?"" So the people informed him: ""They are saying: Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is a righteous servant."
"5871","I remember this about the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), that he had screened me with his cloak and I was watching the Abyssinians who were performing feats in the mosque; at that time, I was a young girl. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This is the last part of the narrations regarding the permissions transmitted from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), which we have dictated in various chapters. Some ahadith related to this category remain, which we will mention in other types, just as we have mentioned them in this category, according to the fundamental methodology by which we have arranged the book. After this category, we will dictate the fifth category of the Sunan, and these are the actions of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), which will be dictated along with their chapters and types, if Allah Almighty so decrees and wills. May Allah Almighty include us among those who are guided to the straight path, granted the ability to follow the correct way, who intended to collect the Sunan and reports, acquired understanding of authentic narrations, and preferred those deeds which can bring them closer to the presence of the Almighty, and preferred them over those things which, in principle, distance from Him. Indeed, He (i.e., Allah Almighty) is the best to be asked."
"5872","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who plays backgammon disobeys Allah and His Apostle. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4938)"
"5876","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and at that time two girls were sitting with him, beating the duff and singing. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was resting with a cloth over his face. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) scolded the two girls, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) removed the cloth from his face and said: O Abu Bakr, let them be, for these are the days of Eid. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Abyssinian delegation came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), they began to perform feats in the mosque. I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) shielding me with his cloak, and I kept watching them as they performed in the mosque until I myself became bored. You can imagine how eager a young girl would be to watch such games and play."
"5877","Abu Bakr came to my house while two small Ansari girls were singing beside me the stories of the Ansar concerning the Day of Buath. And they were not singers. Abu Bakr said protestingly, ""Musical instruments of Satan in the house of Messenger of Allah ﷺ !"" It happened on the ʿId day and Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""O Abu Bakr! There is an ʿId for every nation and this is our ʿId."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 952)"
"5878","The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) came and visited me in the morning when I had been conducted to my husband, and sat on my bedding as you are sitting beside me. Some little girls of ours began to play the tambourine and eulogise those of my ancestors who were killed in the battle of Badr, and then one of them said: And among us is a Prophet who knows what will happen tomorrow. He said : Stop this and say what you were saying. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4922)"
"5879","I came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book, (so) we eat in their utensils, and (live) in a hunting region. where I hunt with, the help of my bow, and hunt with my trained dog, or with my dog which is not trained. So inform me what is lawful (Halal) for us out of that. He (the Holy Prophet) said: Regarding what you have mentioned of the fact that you live in the land belonging to the People of the Book and so you eat in their utensils, but if you can get utensils other than theirs, then don't eat in them; but if you do not find any, then wash them and eat in them. And regarding what you have mentioned about (your living) in a hunting region, what you hunt, (strike) with the help of your bow, recite the name of Allah (while shooting an arrow) and then eat; and what you catch with the help of your trained dog, recite the name of Allah (while letting oil) the dog and then eat it, and what you get with the help of your untrained dog, (if you find it alive) and slaughter it (according to the law of the Shari'ah), eat it. (Using translation from Muslim 1930a)"
"5880","I release my dog and mention the name of Allah, and then another dog joins my dog and both hunt and kill the prey, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Do not eat it, because you do not know whether your dog killed it or the other dog killed it."
"5881","I said: Messenger of Allah, I set off trained dogs and they catch for me (the game) and I recite the name of Allah over it (I slaughter the game by reciting Bismillah-i-Allah-o-Akbar), whereupon he said: When you set off your trained dogs, if you recited the name of Allah (while setting them off), then eat (the game). I said: Even if they (the trained dogs) kill that (the game)? He (the Holy Prophet) said: Even if these kill, but (on the condition) that no other dog, which you did not set off (along with your dogs), participates (in catching the game). I said to him: I throw Mi'rad, a heavy featherless blunt arrow, for hunting and killing (the game). Thereupon he said: When you throw Mi'rad, and it pierces, then eat, but if it falls flatly (and beats the game to death), then do not eat that. (Using translation from Muslim 1929a)"
"5882","The Prophet (peace be upon him) had made shade with a piece of leather. We presented our case to you, and you decided that it would be divided equally between us both. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), sometimes we find some camels among which are milch she-camels whose udders are full of milk, and we are in dire need of it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Call the owner of the camels three times; if he comes, then fine, otherwise milk it and drink, then milk it again, and then leave some milk (in its udder). I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), sometimes another animal comes to us, so if we give it something to drink, will we get a reward for it? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Yes, there is a reward for doing good to every living being. After that, the Prophet (peace be upon him) began to converse with us. He said: Soon a time will come when the best wealth will be sheep that are between two prostrations; they will eat (leaves) from the trees, come to the water, their owner will follow behind them, drink their milk, wear clothes from their wool (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), wear clothes from their hair, while by Allah, tribulations will have spread among the Arabs. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Advise me about this. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Perform prayer, give zakat, fast in Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House of Allah and Umrah, treat your parents well, maintain the rights of kinship, honor the guest, enjoin good, forbid evil, and remain with the truth wherever it may be."
"5883","“Allah has prescribed Al-Ihsan (proficiency) in all things. So if you kill, then kill well, and if you slaughter, then slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3170)"
"5884","“Allah has prescribed Al-Ihsan (proficiency) in all things. So if you kill, then kill well, and if you slaughter, then slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3170)"
"5885","a wolf attacked a sheep so they slaughtered it with a Marwah, and the Prophet allowed it to be eaten. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4407)"
"5886","My grandfather, Rafiʿ said, ""We were in the company of the Prophet ﷺ at DhulHulaifa, and the people suffered from hunger. We got some camels and sheep (as booty) and the Prophet ﷺ was still behind the people. They hurried and put the cooking pots on the fire. (When he came) he ordered that the cooking pots should be upset and then he distributed the booty (amongst the people) regarding ten sheep as equal to one camel then a camel fled and the people chased it till they got tired, as they had a few horses (for chasing it). So a man threw an arrow at it and caused it to stop (with Allah's Permission). On that the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Some of these animals behave like wild beasts, so, if any animal flee from you, deal with it in the same way."" My grandfather asked (the Prophet ﷺ ), ""We hope (or are afraid) that we may meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives. Can we slaughter our animals with canes?"" Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, ""If the instrument used for killing causes the animal to bleed profusely and if Allah's Name is mentioned on killing it, then eat its meat (i.e. it is lawful) but won't use a tooth or a nail and I am telling you the reason: A tooth is a bone (and slaughtering with a bone is forbidden ), and a nail is the slaughtering instrument of the Ethiopians."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3075)"
"5887","narrates: He hunted two rabbits and slaughtered them with a stone. Then he asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about this, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted him to eat both of them."
"5888","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the practice of ""Sharitah"" of Satan. Ikrimah says: The people in the past used to cut off a small part (of the animal) and then leave the animal as it was until it died; they would not cut its veins. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade this practice."
"5889","The Prophet ﷺ said: The slaughter of embryo is included when its mother is slaughtered. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2828)"
"5890","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""There is no significance to Fara’ and ‘Atirah.\"""""
"5891","Sayyiduna Abu Razin (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), saying: We slaughter our animal, then we eat from it and feed whoever comes to us from it. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is no harm in it.(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) These are the sacrifices that people used to perform in the time of ignorance, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) declared them p"
"5892","narrates: Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) had a servant who was grazing his goats near the mountain ""Sala’"". One of the goats was about to die, so the maid could not find a knife to slaughter it, and she slaughtered it with a stone. This matter was presented to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and he (peace be upon him) permitted its meat to be eaten (i.e., he gave permission)."
"5893","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted them to eat the meat of that (goat). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration is transmitted from Nafi’ from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and also from Nafi’ from the son of Sayyiduna Ka’b bin Malik from his father. So all its routes are preserved."
"5894","""I heard Sharid say: 'I herd the Messenger of Allah say: Whoever kills a small bird for no reason, it will beseech Allah on the Day of Resurrection saying: O Lord, so and so killed me for no reason. And he did not kill me for any beneficial purpose.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4446)"
"5895","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""I have been commanded to fight the idolators until they bear witness to La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship except Allah) and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah [SAW]. If they bear witness to La ilaha illallah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah [SAW], and they face our Qiblah, eat our slaughtered animals, and pray as we do, then their blood and wealth become forbidden except for a right that is due, and they will have the same rights and obligations as the Muslims."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3967)"
"5896","narrator says: We found in it this statement: ""May Allah curse the one who sacrifices an animal in the name of other than Allah, and may Allah curse the one who attributes himself to someone other than his real master."
"5897","""Ibn Al-Musayyab told me that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet told him that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever wants to offer a sacrifice, let him not remove anything from his nails or cut his hair for the first ten days Dhul-Jijjah.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4362)"
"5898","“You sacrifice it yourself.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3138)"
"5899","I brought it to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), this is a six-month-old kid."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""You may sacrifice it."
"5900","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice two horned, black-and-white rams and he would say the Name of Allah and pronounce His greatness. I saw him slaughtering them with his own hand, putting his foot on their sides.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3120)"
"5901","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice two horned, black-and-white rams and he would say the Name of Allah and pronounce His greatness. I saw him slaughtering them with his own hand, putting his foot on their sides.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3120)"
"5902","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice a choice, horned ram with black round the eyes, the mouth and the feet. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2796)"
"5903","I was present with Ibn ʿUmar at Minah. He passed a man who was sacrificing his camel while it was sitting. He said make it stand and tie its leg ; thus follow the practice (sunnah) of Muhammad (SWAS). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1768)"
"5904","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We offered as sacrifice a six-month-old sheep in the presence of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)."""
"5905","Sayyiduna Abu"
"5906","""The Prophet ﷺ delivered a Khutbah on the day of An-Nahr and said: 'The first thing we start with on this day of ours is the prayer, then we offer sacrifice. Whoever does that, he has followed our sunnah, but whoever slaughtered (his sacrifice) before the (prayer), that is just meat that he gave to his family. Abu Burdah bin Niyar had slaughtered his sacrifice and he said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I have a Jadha'ah that is better than a Musinnah.' He said: 'Slaughter it (as a sacrifice), but that will not be sufficient for anyone else (as a sacrifice) after you.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1563)"
"5907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “You may offer it in its place, but after you, it will not be permissible for anyone else.”"
"5908","He who observes prayer like our prayer and turns his face towards our Qibla (in prayer) and who offers sacrifices (of animals) as we do, he must not slaughter the (animal as a sacrifice) until he has completed the prayer. Thereupon my maternal uncle said: Messenger of Allah, I have sacrificed the animal on behalf of my son. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is the thing in which you have made haste for your family. He said: I have a goat with me better than two goats. Thereupon he said: Sacrifice it for that is the best. (Using translation from Muslim 1961d)"
"5909","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: After you, it will not be permissible for anyone to slaughter an animal before performing the prayer."
"5910","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us on the day of sacrifice after the prayer. He said: If anyone prays like our prayer, and sacrifices like our sacrifice, his sacrifice is all right. If anyone sacrifices before the prayer (for 'Id), that is goat meant for flesh. Abu Burdah b. Niyar stood up and said: Messenger of Allah, I swear by Allah, I sacrificed before I went for prayer. I thought it was the day of eating and drinking; so I made haste, and ate myself, and supplied flesh to my family and neighbors. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: That is a goat meant for eating flesh. He said: I have a kid (of less than a year) which is better than two goats meant for flesh. Will it be valid from me ? He said: Yes, but it will not be valid for anyone after you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2800)"
"5911","I have a six-month-old kid goat which is better than a one-year-old animal. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be sufficient for you, but it will not be sufficient for anyone after you."
"5912","narrates: He sacrificed an animal before going for the Eid prayer, then he mentioned this to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered him to sacrifice again."
"5913","""We slaughtered the sacrifice with the Messenger of Allah on day, and the people slaughtered their sacrifices before the prayer. When he finished (the prayer) the Prophet saw that they had slaughtered their sacrifices before the prayer. He said: ""Whoever slaughtered his sacrifice before the prayer, let him slaughter another in its place, and whoever did not slaughter his sacrifice until we had prayed, let him slaughter it in the name of Allah, The Mighty and Sublime,"" (Sahih ) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4398)"
"5914","""I have been instructed to take the Day of Sacrifice as an 'Id which Allah, the Might and Sublime, has ordained for this Ummah."" The man said: ""What do you think if I cannot find anything but a female sheep that has been loaned to me so that I may benefit from its milk - should I sacrifice it?"" He said: ""No. Rather cut something from your hair and your nails, trim your mustache and shave your pubic hairs, and you will have a complete reward with Allah, the Might and Sublime, as if you had offered the sacrifice."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4365)"
"5915","The Prophet ﷺ ordered a horned ram with black legs, black belly and black round the eyes, and it was brought from him to sacrifice. He said: 'Aishah, get the knife then he said: Sharpen it with a stone. So I did. He took it, then take the ram he placed it on the ground and slaughtered it. He then said: In the name of Allah. O Allah, accept it for Muhammad, Muhammad's family and Muhammad's people. Then he sacrificed it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2792)"
"5916","that Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""If anyone of you has seen the crescent of Dhū al-Ḥijjah and one of you want to offer a sacrifice ˹on the Day of Naḥr˺, then he should hold back ˹cutting˺ his hair and nails."" (Using translation from Muslim 1977e)"
"5917","He who has a sacrificial animal with him whom (he intends) to offer as sacrifice, and he enters the month of Dhu'I-Hijja, he should not get his hair cut or nails trimmed until he has sacrificed the animal. (Using translation from Muslim 1977g)"
"5918","I met Sa'id bin al-Musayyib and mentioned this matter to him, so he said: O my nephew, this hadith has been forgotten. Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) has informed me of this: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the (first) ten days (of Dhul-Hijjah) begin and any one of you has an animal for sacrifice which he intends to offer, then he should not cut his hair or nails until he has offered the sacrifice."
"5919","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin ‘Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) that while mentioning sacrifice, he stated that the Noble Prophet (peace and b"
"5920","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine the eyes and ears (of the sacrificial animals)."
"5921","""I heard the Messenger of Allah say"" - and he gestured with his fingers, but his fingers were shorter than the fingers of the Messenger of Allah - he said ""It is not permissible to offer as a sacrifice an animal that clearly has one bad eye, a lame animal that is obviously lame, as sick animal that is obviously sick, or an animals that is so emaciated that it is as if there is no marrow in its bones."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4371)"
"5922","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'The sacrifice of four types of animals is not permissible: a one-eyed animal whose defect is obvious, a lame animal whose lameness is obvious, a sick animal whose sickness is obvious, and an animal whose leg is broken and which has no marrow in its body.'"
"5923","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say, ""No one should eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal for more than three days."
"5924","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""No person should eat from his sacrificial animal (meat) for more than three days."
"5925","the Messenger of Allah forbade eating the meat of the sacrificial animals after three days then he said: ""Eat, take some with you (if traveling). And store some."" ( Sahih) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4426)"
"5926","the Messenger of Alllah forbade (Eating) the meat of sacrificial animals after three days. Then Qatadh bin An-Nu' man, who was brother of Abu Sa'eed through his mo0ther, and had been present at Badr, came and they offered him (some of the meat) .He said: ""Didn't the Messenger of Allah forbid it?"" Abu Sa eed said: ""Something happened later. The Messenger of Allah forbade us to eat it for more than three days, then he allowed us to eat it and store it."" (Sahih ) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4428)"
"5927","I mentioned this narration to Amrah bint Abdur Rahman, so she informed me: I heard Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrate that once, during the sacred era of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), on the occasion of Eid al-Adha, some people from the villages came. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You may store (i.e., the meat of the sacrifice) for only three days; whatever remains after that, give it in charity. The female narrator named Amrah says: Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) informed that after this, it was submitted to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): O Messenger of Allah! Previously, people used to benefit from their sacrificial animals; they would preserve their fat and make water skins from their (hides). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: What has happened now? The people said: O Messenger of Allah! You forbade the use of sacrificial meat after three days (so now people do not do so). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I forbade you because of the arrival of those (poor people) who had come to you. Now you may eat it, give it in charity, and store it as well. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The word ""dāfah"" means the group that came to ask (for charity)."
"5928","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O people of Madinah, do not eat the meat of your sacrificial animals for more than three days. The narrator states: The people complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that they had children and servants, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Eat it, feed others with it, and also store it."
"5929","I wanted you to help them in this matter. Now you may eat, feed others, and store it as well.”"
"5930","narrates: We ate dried meat along with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we reached Madinah (that is, we kept the sacrificial meat preserved as provisions for the journey)."
"5931","narrates: We kept the meat of the sacrificial animal as provisions along with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and we continued to use it until we reached Madinah Munawwarah."
"5932","I preserved it, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to use that meat until he reached Madinah Munawwarah."",""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ  said to me"",""'Repair the meat of this sacrificial animal.' So I repaired it"","" and he continued to eat from it until he reached the city."""""""
"5933","narrates: His wife Umm Sulaym asked Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about the meat of the sacrificial animal. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied that Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) returned from a battle and went to his wife, who presented the meat of the sacrificial animal before him. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) refused to eat it until he had asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about it. (When he asked the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him,) the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You may eat it from one Dhul-Hijjah to the next Dhul-Hijjah."
"5934","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A pledge is not binding unless its benefit goes to the person and its liability remains upon him."
"5935","“A mount may be ridden when it is pawned, and its milk may be drunk when it is pawned, but the one who rides it or milks it must pay for its upkeep.' ” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2440)"
"5936","""The Messenger of Allah died when his shield was in pledge with a Jew for thirty Sa's of barley for his family (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4651)"
"5937","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) mortgaged his armor with a Jew in exchange for one dinar. After that, he did not have enough means to pay off the debt and retrieve it, until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away."
"5938","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) bought grain from a Jew on the condition that he would pay him after a year. The Prophet (peace be upon him) left his iron armor with him as collateral."
"5939","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Verbally abusing a Muslim is immorality and fighting him is Kufr (disbelief).'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 69)"
"5940","“Make the people pay attention.” Then he said: “Do not turn back into disbelievers after I am gone, striking one another’s necks.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3942)"
"5941","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Iblis has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but he will create discord among you."
"5942","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever helps his people in an unjust matter, his example is like that of a camel which falls into a well and is then pulled out by its tail."
"5943","I not forbid you from this? Sheathe them and meet your brother."
